WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.868
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Charlie Day.

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.504
The movie comes out
right before Valentine's Day.

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.839
Do you historically
enjoy Valentine's Day?

00:00:06.839 --> 00:00:09.041
-No.
-Yeah.

00:00:09.041 --> 00:00:10.577
-No, it's the worst.

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:13.246
First of all, okay,
if you're in a relationship,

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:15.581
there's an extraordinary amount
of pressure,

00:00:15.581 --> 00:00:17.549
like, "Oh, I got to make sure
I do flowers,

00:00:17.549 --> 00:00:18.752
get the perfect date."

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:20.487
Let's be honest.
It's a pain in the ass.

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:22.255
If you're not in a relationship,

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:23.790
it's just a slap in the face,
right?

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:27.293
It's just like everyone's out
there being happy and in love.

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:29.562
So it's the assface of holidays,
in my opinion.

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:30.997
-Yeah.

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:33.599
You've been with your beautiful
wife, Mary Elizabeth,

00:00:33.599 --> 00:00:35.067
for a really long time.

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:38.037
Is there still an expectation
that you're going to deliver?

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:39.772
-Yeah, that's the problem.

00:00:39.772 --> 00:00:42.241
You know, like, yeah.
And we keep doing it.

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:45.544
Even as a child,
I found it the worst.

00:00:45.544 --> 00:00:47.881
Like, you know, you'd be in,
like, third grade,

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:49.181
and people would be
passing things,

00:00:49.181 --> 00:00:50.716
and you'd get a little thing
and you'd be like,

00:00:50.716 --> 00:00:52.418
"Okay, I got to open it."

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:55.688
And it says, "You have freckles
and are ugly."

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:57.056
Oh, what the --
You know, like --

00:00:57.056 --> 00:00:58.791
-Yeah.
Just write it in a note.

00:00:58.791 --> 00:01:00.460
Don't make it a machine.
-Don't make a whole --

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.462
Yeah, why do I have to
do the whole bit?

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:04.897
"5, 2, 4, 3.

00:01:04.897 --> 00:01:07.266
You smell like farts."

00:01:07.266 --> 00:01:08.901
It's no good.
-Very unkind.

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:11.204
-Very unkind. Even cruel.
-Kids are cruel.

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:13.873
We also had something in common
about our schooling days.

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.675
We both had parents
who were teachers.

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:17.443
Our moms were teachers
at the schools we went to.

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:19.045
-My mom taught music.
What'd your mom teach?

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:20.146
-French.
-Wow.

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:24.217
-Yeah.
How did you like it?

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:25.884
-I think it was sweet, you know,

00:01:25.884 --> 00:01:27.686
when I was little,
in kindergarten.

00:01:27.686 --> 00:01:29.121
Mommy's not too far away.

00:01:29.121 --> 00:01:31.324
By like third grade,
I had lots of trips

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:33.693
to the principal's office,
courtesy of my mother.

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:34.827
-Really?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:35.895
-She sent you?

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:37.997
-I think she made
an example out of me,

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:40.567
which was like, you know, kids
like to goof off in music class.

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:42.401
So I'd be like coming in.
I'd sit down.

00:01:42.401 --> 00:01:44.404
I'd make, like, a joke.
She'd be like, "You, gone!"

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:45.738
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:49.007
You know, and the other kids
were like, "Whoa, man.

00:01:49.007 --> 00:01:51.443
Mrs. Day means business."

00:01:51.443 --> 00:01:53.546
-My mom was a pushover.
-Was she?

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:55.514
-I would get away with anything.
-How un-French.

00:01:55.514 --> 00:01:57.683
-What?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.683 --> 00:01:59.752
She's like [French accent]
"Oh, we cannot."

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.087
-[ French accent ] It's fine.

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:02.755
You can learn it.
You cannot learn it.

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:03.957
-[ French accent ]
You are children.

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:06.492
You are meant to misbehave.

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:10.997
-[ French accent ] They are
just exploring their humor.

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:13.365
-[ Normal voice ]
What was it like at the end --

00:02:13.365 --> 00:02:16.503
when you went home on a night
where you'd been sent

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:18.171
to the principal
by your mom in the day?

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:21.073
-Totally fair, because she was
absolutely right to send me.

00:02:21.073 --> 00:02:22.308
-Okay, got you.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:24.343
So you didn't
hold it against her.

00:02:24.343 --> 00:02:26.446
-No, there was, like,
eye contact.

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:28.380
And be like, "Yeah, I get it."
-Yeah.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:31.217
-"You did the right thing.
I get it. I get it.

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:33.019
Strong move, Mom."
-Alright, that's good.

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:36.121
You respected the game.
-I did. I did, yeah.

00:02:36.121 --> 00:02:37.390
-Everybody says that about you.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:39.292
-Yeah, I respect my mother.

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:40.893
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:43.062
Class act.

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:44.497
-You have not been doing it
very long,

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:45.497
but it's already very popular.

00:02:45.497 --> 00:02:46.999
You're doing a "Sunny" podcast.

00:02:46.999 --> 00:02:51.204
And this is the cast
is rewatching episodes.

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:53.773
And so this is
a situation where,

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:55.007
obviously, you watched them
when you made them,

00:02:55.007 --> 00:02:56.876
because you were a creator
of the show,

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:58.578
but going back
and watching them again,

00:02:58.578 --> 00:02:59.779
do you remember everything,

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:02.548
or is there sort of a joy
of discovery going back?

00:03:02.548 --> 00:03:04.617
-I don't remember anything.

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:06.986
And it's real sad.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:09.522
Like, I think the other guys
remember everything,

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:11.290
and I think they're all
worried about me.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:12.558
-Okay.
-Yeah.

00:03:12.558 --> 00:03:14.927
But, no, it's good.

00:03:14.927 --> 00:03:16.095
It's good to --

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:17.764
I sort of feel like
they all hold up.

00:03:17.764 --> 00:03:19.365
I go in thinking they're
not going to be good.

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:20.700
Be like, "Oh, boy, here we go."

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.201
And I think the show
really holds up.

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:24.037
I'm proud of it.
-That's fantastic.

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:25.471
To do something like that
that holds up,

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:27.173
I mean, what more
can you ask for?

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:28.808
-That's the goal, you know?
-That's the goal.

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:29.976
-That's the goal.

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:31.210
-This is your first time
back in New York City

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:33.379
since this whole thing started.

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:35.848
-This is, yeah.
I've not been here.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.049
I've not been invited.

00:03:37.049 --> 00:03:38.250
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:39.251
-Lorne?
-No.

00:03:39.251 --> 00:03:40.485
-Lorne hasn't called?

00:03:40.485 --> 00:03:41.987
-Lorne has not called.

00:03:41.987 --> 00:03:43.555
He has not called.
But he will.

00:03:43.555 --> 00:03:45.157
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-I'm keeping up hope.

00:03:45.157 --> 00:03:46.825
Although, he's retiring?

00:03:46.825 --> 00:03:47.827
-No.

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:49.328
-He's not going?
-I don't believe it.

00:03:49.328 --> 00:03:50.462
-After 50?

00:03:50.462 --> 00:03:52.632
-He says after 50,
he's going to retire.

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:54.500
-Okay.
-No.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.935
-I think I could do it.

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:58.237
-You want to take over?
-I could take over.

00:03:58.237 --> 00:03:59.238
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:00.739
-I mean, when you
think about it --

00:04:00.739 --> 00:04:03.542
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you, thank you.

00:04:03.542 --> 00:04:06.078
-Nobody's talking about you,
but when you think about it,

00:04:06.078 --> 00:04:08.614
he's at whatever --
he's at like 47.

00:04:08.614 --> 00:04:11.250
You guys are the next-
longest-running comedy show.

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:13.919
-Yeah, so we're basically
doing the same thing.

00:04:13.919 --> 00:04:15.287
I could like...

00:04:15.287 --> 00:04:17.289
-Oh, that's good.

00:04:17.289 --> 00:04:19.025
-Now I got to do an impression.

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:21.460
Shoot.
I backed myself into a corner.

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:22.528
-Yeah, yeah, do it.

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:23.863
-[ As Lorne Michaels ]
He was funny.

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:25.565
That's about it.
Everyone does it.

00:04:25.565 --> 00:04:27.733
-Can you do him
and De Niro talking?

00:04:27.733 --> 00:04:30.035
-Oh, boy.
So it'd be like...

00:04:30.035 --> 00:04:31.937
[ As Robert De Niro ]
You gonna put him on the show?

00:04:31.937 --> 00:04:33.172
Put him back on the show?

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:34.941
[ As Lorne Michaels ]
Mm, no, Bobby.

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:36.075
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:38.410
[ Applause ]
-That was really good.

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:39.712
-[ Normal voice ] I didn't know
I was going to do that.

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:41.080
That was not a planned bit.
-I want to make it clear.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:42.648
That was not discussed
ahead of time.

00:04:42.648 --> 00:04:44.350
I fully put you on the spot.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.251
And I want you to know,

00:04:46.251 --> 00:04:48.321
that's me having a lot of
respect and confidence in you.

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:51.123
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
That was a foolish move.

00:04:51.123 --> 00:04:52.525
-I wouldn't do that
to a lot of guests.

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:54.293
-Not a master impressionist.

00:04:54.293 --> 00:04:56.929
'Cause I always sound like this,
and that's the problem.

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:58.130
-Well, that's the thing.

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:00.133
Everybody says you do
the best Charlie Day.

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:02.601
-Spot-on.
Spot-on. Yeah.

00:05:02.601 --> 00:05:05.437
You know, I did have someone
stop me once in the airport,

00:05:05.437 --> 00:05:07.907
and I think they heard me
talking and they came up to me

00:05:07.907 --> 00:05:10.409
and they go, "Are you you?"

00:05:10.409 --> 00:05:13.145
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.145 --> 00:05:18.684
And I thought about it.
I was like, "Am I me?"

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:22.287
I said, "You know, no, I'm just
not feeling like myself today."

00:05:22.287 --> 00:05:25.457
And, yeah, but that was the
oddest one -- "Are you you?"

00:05:25.457 --> 00:05:27.392
-I got one
my first year on "SNL,"

00:05:27.392 --> 00:05:29.962
so, again, I wasn't well-known,
but I'm at a bar.

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:31.997
I was at a bar in Milwaukee,
and somebody came up to me

00:05:31.997 --> 00:05:35.268
and said, "You look like
that guy on 'SNL.'"

00:05:35.268 --> 00:05:38.904
And I said, "I am."
Because, again, I was new on TV.

00:05:38.904 --> 00:05:39.939
I was so excited.

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:42.408
I said, "I am that guy
on 'SNL.'"

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:44.210
And he looked at me and went
"[Bleep] you."

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:47.446
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.446 --> 00:05:48.914
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:48.914 --> 00:05:51.050
This [bleep] guy, man.

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:53.118
-"Don't go in the bar right now.
There's a [bleep] [bleep]"

00:05:53.118 --> 00:05:54.387
-Yeah, seriously.

00:05:54.387 --> 00:05:55.587
-"Trying to get me
to buy him a free drink

00:05:55.587 --> 00:05:57.456
'cause he's new on 'SNL.'"

00:05:57.456 --> 00:05:58.824
Well, thank you for being here.

00:05:58.824 --> 00:06:01.360
-Oh, my pleasure.
You kicking me out?

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:03.562
-I don't want you to think of it
like that.

00:06:03.562 --> 00:06:06.098
-Okay.
-It's just -- But yes.

00:06:06.098 --> 00:06:07.666
-You got Sam here.
-We got Sam here.

00:06:07.666 --> 00:06:08.801
We got other A-listers.

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:10.002
-I don't want to go
into Sam's time.

00:06:10.002 --> 00:06:11.336
He's the best.
-Yeah, alright, good.

00:06:11.336 --> 00:06:13.272
That's very big of you.
-Thanks for having me, man.

00:06:13.272 --> 00:06:15.774
-It's great to have you.
-I'll see you on the beach?

00:06:15.774 --> 00:06:17.210
-Charlie Day, everybody.

